Preventive care identifies health issues early, allowing for more effective and less costly treatments.
Studies show that populations with higher access to preventive services experience lower rates of severe illness and mortality.
By addressing risk factors before they develop into serious conditions, preventive care reduces long-term healthcare costs.
Preventive measures like vaccinations have been proven to drastically reduce the spread of infectious diseases.
Maintaining good health through preventive care leads to increased productivity and fewer missed workdays.